# Intro version line (date vs version)

## Date — update on every project update

Whenever you complete work that updates this app (features, fixes, copy, data, etc.), refresh the **date** in the welcome intro:

- **Where:** `src/FernIdentifier.tsx` → `INTRO_LINES` → the entry shaped like `'Version 0.3  5Apr26'`.
- **What to change:** only the **`DDMonYY`** suffix to **today’s real calendar date** (e.g. `5Apr26`).
- **Do not** skip this after substantive edits.

## Version number — only when explicitly requested

- **Do not** change the semantic version (`0.3`, `0.3.0`, etc.) on routine updates.
- Change **`package.json`** `version`, **`package-lock.json`** root `version`, and the **`Version X.Y`** part of that `INTRO_LINES` string **only when the user explicitly asks** to update or bump the version (e.g. “set version to 0.4”).
- When the user **does** ask for a version bump, update all of those places together and still set the intro **date** to today.

## Format

- Intro line pattern: `'Version X.Y  DDMonYY'` (two spaces before the date, same style as existing entries).
